                        is the half of the tile that colour is not allowed to
                        carry alone. A second line costs 14px; a lost word costs
                        the rule. */}
                    <span class:list={['block text-xs leading-tight', t.labelClass]}>
                      {t.label}
                    </span>
                  </span>
                  {/*
                    A second, non-colour signal for which tile is on. The dark
                    ring does the work for most people, but "selected" carried by
                    an outline alone is the kind of state that disappears in
                    sunlight on a cracked phone screen in a yard — which is
                    precisely where this gets read.

                    On track says what it is instead: nothing to open.
                  */}
                  <span
                    class:list={[
                      // 11px, not 10px, and ink-700 rather than ink-300: this
                      // is the line that says which filter is on, and it was
                      // set at 1.85:1 on a tile read in daylight.
                      'mt-0.5 block text-[11px] leading-tight',
                      t.view === null
                        ? 'text-emerald-800'
